{"status":"completed","summary":"node1 now has a persistent firewalld policy permitting SSH and TCP/8080 while rejecting unrelated inbound connections. The policy and traffic behavior remained correct after a verified node restart.","actions_performed":["Kept SSH enabled in the public zone and added TCP/8080 permanently.","Removed the Cockpit and DHCPv6-client allowances.","Verified the terminal nftables rule rejects unmatched inbound traffic.","Tested SSH and TCP/8080 acceptance and TCP/8081 rejection using isolated ingress.","Safely restarted node1 and confirmed its boot identity changed.","Removed all temporary test interfaces, namespaces, listeners, and files."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Persistent firewall permits only SSH and TCP/8080 and rejects unrelated inbound connections","command_ids":["cmd-6dfb9833889342dd","cmd-6d483c5612a74dc6","cmd-6bc969212cc94bfb"],"summary":"Runtime and permanent policy show SSH plus 8080/tcp, Cockpit/9090 absent, and an admin-prohibited reject terminator. With live listeners on both test ports, SSH returned its banner, 8080 returned HTTP 200, and inbound 8081 was rejected while its local control request returned HTTP 200."},{"requirement":"node1 mandatory restart and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-d7f3c378f616494d","cmd-8ba711ce9a3f48bf","cmd-6fca16c8d52b4b81","cmd-cb117f312a8a45d3","cmd-7b86313c1e8341c1","cmd-a469c783317143f6","cmd-686ef2a2a5ce4fa3"],"summary":"Pre-restart boot ID f38484ef-a289-4d30-9a94-4ab42c44f900 had healthy firewalld/sshd and the intended policy. The safe restart was acknowledged, and the boot ID changed to f22aaa3c-303a-4ce0-b8d9-20a4a2a29de8. After recovery, firewalld and sshd were active, the persistent policy was restored, SSH and 8080 worked, unrelated 8081 remained rejected, and all test artifacts were absent."}]}
